From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jasmine <jasmine@localhost>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 01:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] jasmine-j0133: trace queued swaps, the presenter and display power (diagnostic)

Diagnostic only. The GPU accessor is guarded until its window is mapped (the trace records from AppleCLCD::start(), before gpudelay). The clean-j0132 log netlog-revert.txt
4490-4830 is the primary case: swap 191 was ADMITTED (accepted 191) but
fShownID/fEndID/fProgramSerial stayed 189, while fQueueWaiting and
fPresentBusy were both 0. So the presenter had already consumed and dropped
the accepted record (or never re-armed for it), and its thread was parked.
The 64-entry ring now records the whole path, including every presenter
wakeup and every queuePresent exit, so the drop reason and the parked state
are visible without any other log.

Per-swap lines (all carry id and ser, the token serial, from the ACCEPT map):
  BEGIN     SwapBegin: id, serial, epoch, queue mode.
  ADMIT     swap(): SwapEnd decision. t = SwapEnd entry time; ms = time to
            the decision; cand = queueCandidate(); tok = token found; wr =
            a layer has displayWriters; avail = queue/present slot free;
            outcome = queued/sync/direct/pending/reject/abort/sync-timeout/
            ticket-fail/latch-fail; reason is the rejectFrame reason.
  ACCEPT    fAcceptedSerial was advanced: id, serial, epoch, mode=queue/sync,
            accepted/waiting/busy, q=fQueueActive, tickets bitmap, per-layer
            gpuSeqno, layer mask.
  QP-ENTER  queuePresent() acquired the present scope (fPresentBusy set):
            age = ms since this swap's SwapEnd, tickets, point-in-time seq.
  QP-TICKET-WAIT
            one line per ticket/GPU-seqno poll: first poll, every 100 ms, or
            when the lagging-layer mask changes. done = sweet_gpu_completed(),
            wait = ms since the poll loop started, lag = layers still behind,
            tickets = layers with a retained ticket, seq = per-layer seqno.
  QP-TICKET the admission loop ended: ready, err, wait ms, final lag mask.
  QP-CANCEL the ticket-cancel quiesce loop (only when a ticket was cancelled)
            ended: cancelled, quiesced, wait ms, ticket mask.
  WAITLATCH waitLatch() entered (phase 0), polled (phase 1, every 100 ms
            while fLatchValid), or returned (phase 2, got): pending, latch,
            ctl/flush, wait ms, fQueueWaiting/fPresentBusy.
  QP-LATCH  waitLatch() returned at the queuePresent call site: got, wait ms,
            pending, latch/latched/program, ctl/flush.
  QP-PROG   scanScaled() programmed VIG0: surf/seq, pa/stride, scan ms, ctl.
  QP-DROP   queuePresent() computed a drop: reason, ready, cancelled,
            latched, epochok.
  QP-EXIT   every queuePresent() return: reason code (below), valid/ready/
            cancelled/quiesced/latched/epochok/terminal flags, active =
            fQueueActive, accepted = fAcceptedSerial, waiting/busy AFTER the
            queue state was cleared, wait ms, ticket mask, shown/end/latch/
            latchedSer/program, mask. This is the line that explains an
            accepted swap that was never programmed.
  NOTE      noteShown(): fEndID/fLatchValid/fShownValid/fLatchID, ctl/flush,
            fLatchedSerial/fProgramSerial after the call.
  RETIRE-WAIT retireLatched() at each 50 ms retry while the latch is pending
            and CTL_FLUSH is still set; wait ms, retry, latchValid, ctl/flush.
  RETIRE-OK retireLatched() retired: by=ctl-clear or timeout; wait ms, ctl/
            flush, latchValid after, latch id, shown/end, latched/program.
  FALLBACK  queueFallback(): reason, swap, serial, epoch, latchValid/latch,
            ctl/flush, latched/program, accepted/waiting/busy.

QP-EXIT reason codes:
  0  valid and programmed (scanScaled/noteShown completed)
  2  GPU seqno/ticket not ready at the deadline (queueFallback reason 2)
  3  ready but the record was no longer valid (latch/epoch/candidate/terminal
     or queue off; queueFallback reason 3)
  13 a ticket was cancelled and its backing was quiesced; dropped without a
     fallback (this is the likely cause of an accepted swap disappearing)
  20 terminal() after scanScaled but before noteShown; queuePresent returns
     without clearing fQueueWaiting (early return)

Presenter lines:
  PRESENTER phase=1 start, 2 start-fail, 3 thread entry, 4 park-before-sleep,
  5 wake-after-sleep, 6 non-protocol fQLock park, 7 non-protocol fQLock wake.
  cond = (fQueueWaiting ? 1 : 0) | (fPresentBusy ? 2 : 0); accepted = the
  serial seen; fSerial/epoch/shown/end/latch/latched/program are the state.
  The thread has no exit: presenter() has two infinite for(;;) loops and
  presenterMain() calls it forever. It can block indefinitely in
  queuePresent()'s IOLockSleep(fLock, fQueueRec) (no timeout) and in the
  non-protocol IOLockSleep(fQLock, fQRec) (no timeout); waitLatch() also has
  no timeout (it polls every 1 ms and relies on retireLatched's 150 ms
  fallback). When fQueueWaiting == 0 and fPresentBusy == 0 the presenter is
  parked at the queuePresent condvar unless it has already exited.
  Ticket/GPU waits are bounded (100 ms untracked, 1000 ms tracked); the
  cancel quiesce is bounded at 100 ms; drainPresent's slot wait at 200 ms.

Display power lines:
  POWER phase=0 enter, 1 exit, 2 drain failure, 3 off ignored by sweetfb_stayon.
  Fields: off, changed, owned (drainPresent owns the present scope), ret,
  powerOff/fPowerOff, ep/fEpoch, active/fQueueActive, busy/fPresentBusy,
  waiting/fQueueWaiting, accepted/fAcceptedSerial, suspended/
  sweet_ticket_suspended, tokens (live fTokens), qtickets (fQueueTicket),
  repoch/sweet_render_epoch, shown/end/latch/latchValid/latched/program, ctl/flush.
  DRAIN phase=0 waiting for !fPresentBusy && !fQueueWaiting, 1 scope owned,
  2 waitLatch returned true, 3 waitLatch false (releasePresent), 4 200 ms
  timeout.

What the power path resets (none of it is the framebuffer queue state):
  display off: sweet_ticket_cancel(NULL) increments sweet_render_epoch, sets
  sweet_ticket_suspended = true, marks every live ticket status=2/cancelled,
  decrements live, increments aborts, and wakes fQueueRec. It does not change
  fEpoch, fQueueActive, fAcceptedSerial, fProgramSerial, fLatchedSerial,
  fLatchValid/fLatchID or fPresentBusy/fQueueWaiting.
  Then drainPresent() waits for the presenter (200 ms) and takes the present
  scope; it only retires a latch through waitLatch().
  display on: clears sweet_ticket_suspended; it does not reset fEpoch, the
  token table, the queue, the accepted/program serials or the latch. The
  cancelled tickets stay cancelled.
  The only framebuffer state changed is fPowerOff, fFadeStep=0 and fDirty=1.
  A QUEUE FALLBACK reason 1 after display on comes from the synchronous
  admission loop in AppleCLCD::swap(): after 200 ms without a free present
  slot, rejectFrame(id, 1) -> queueFallback(1); the ADMIT line shows
  reason=1 and the following FALLBACK line shows the swap/serial and the
  power/latch state.

The latch/retire condition is unchanged: pending = fLatchValid ||
fLatchID != 0; it reads CTL_FLUSH only (fCtl0[0x18/4], not a vsync count)
and retires when that register AND fFlushMask is zero, or after 150 ms in
queue mode / 50 ms in sync mode. In queue mode it logs RETIRE-WAIT at 50 ms
retries and calls queueFallback(6) at 150 ms; a timeout retirement does not
advance fLatchedSerial or fShownValid, so queue-mode SwapWait
(fLatchedSerial > serial) cannot complete.

Every entry also carries c = sweet_gpu_completed() and s = sweet_gpu_seqno()
(last seqno sweet_gpu_submit assigned; read-only accessor in
bsd/dev/sweet_gpu.c), so Maps' work ahead of the display's own swaps is
visible.

Dump: automatic on the first j0132 swapWait stuck and on queueFallback; on
demand with command-port "fb trace" (bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c, after j0131's
"smp"). Output is bounded at 64 entry lines plus the header and state line.
t is ms since the first entry; c/s are decimal seqnos; masks/ctl are hex.
No IOLog happens while fLock is held. The entry ring is lock free (an atomic
write index plus per-slot seqlock stamps), so recording never blocks and no
trace helper takes fLock; nothing is recorded before AppleCLCD::start has
allocated fLock. sweet_gpu_completed() returns 0 until the GPU thread has
mapped its window, because the first PRESENTER entry is recorded in start()
before gpudelay elapses.

